[55.683237, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read().replace('`steps` in deletion order.', '''`steps` in deletion order. Teardown selects resources with an exact matching branch tag\nor `stack_id = stk-<branch>`, including untagged boot volumes. It deletes dependents\nbefore their dependencies, refuses teardown when resources outside the selection still\ndepend on it, and rejects dependency cycles before deleting anything.\n\nLegacy resources with neither a branch tag nor a stack ID must be identified from\nprovisioning/teardown records and cleaned up separately by verified ID. Do not use broad\nuntagged garbage collection to tear down a branch: unrelated resources may be untagged.''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nset -o pipefail\nbin/envctl teardown --branch feat-ledger 2>&1 | tee ops/logs/teardown-feat-ledger-2026-11-22.log\n"]
