[63.515523, "o", "# envctl\r\n\r\nCLI for per-branch preview environments on Nimbus (our cloud provider). Every feature branch\r\ngets a stack `stk-<branch>` with its own network, instances, load balancer and DNS name;\r\n`envctl teardown` removes it when the branch merges.\r\n\r\n    envctl list                          # resources and cost per branch\r\n    envctl plan --branch feat-x [--json] # what teardown would delete, in order\r\n    envctl teardown --branch feat-x      # delete the branch environment\r\n    envctl gc --untagged [--yes]         # delete untagged resources\r\n\r\n`plan --json` prints `{\"branch\", \"steps\": [{\"id\", \"type\", \"name\"}], \"blocked\": [...]}` with\r\n`steps` in deletion order.\r\n\r\nCredentials come from `ENVCTL_TOKEN` or `~/.envctl/credentials` (`token = ...`); the API URL\r\nfrom `ENVCTL_API` (default `http://127.0.0.1:8900`). API reference: `docs/cloud-api.md`.\r\n\r\nRuns on Node 22 with type stripping, no dependencies.\r\n\r\n    npm test\r\n"]
[63.515971, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@ffcb50654e90:/app# "]
[63.651923, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read().replace('`steps` in deletion order.', '''`steps` in deletion order. Teardown selects resources with an exact matching branch tag\nor `stack_id = stk-<branch>`, including untagged boot volumes. It deletes dependents\nbefore their dependencies, refuses teardown when resources outside the selection still\ndepend on it, and rejects dependency cycles before deleting anything.\n\nLegacy resources with neither a branch tag nor a stack ID must be identified from\nprovisioning/teardown records and cleaned up separately by verified ID. Do not use broad\nuntagged garbage collection to tear down a branch: unrelated resources may be untagged.''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nset -o pipefail\nbin/envctl teardown --branch feat-ledger 2>&1 | tee ops/logs/teardown-feat-ledger-2026-11-22.log\n"]
[63.653188, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> p='README.md'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> s=open(p).read().replace('`steps` in deletion order.', '''`steps` in deletion order. Teardown selects resources with an exact matching branch tag\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> or `stack_id = stk-<branch>`, including untagged boot volumes. It deletes dependents\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> before their dependencies, refuses teardown when resources outside the selection still\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> depend on it, and rejects dependency cycles before deleting anything.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Legacy resources with neither a branch tag nor a stack ID must be identified from\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> provisioning/teardown records and cleaned up separately by verified ID. Do not use broad\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[63.653423, "o", "untagged garbage collection to tear down a branch: unrelated resources may be untagged.''')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> open(p,'w').write(s)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> PY\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
